<!--
    WhatsNewWindow – the release timeline (Paper "v11 · Conduit What's New — sunflower on the rail",
    plus "v10 · hover — preview card" and "v10 · click — large view").

    This file is only the LOOK. It contains no release text at all: every word comes from Changelog.json,
    which WhatsNewWindow.xaml.cs reads when the window opens. A new release = a new block in that file, nothing here.

        ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
        │   ✿  NEWEST FIRST        What's new                          ● You're on 0.1.0                 │  page header
        │   │╲                                                                                           │  (the sunflower)
        │  ◖│  November 12, 2026   One switch for single and multiple tests.            ·                │  ┐
        │   ┃  0.1.0               Choose how you want to run …                         ·                │  │
        │   ┃  (•Feature)                                                               ·                │  │
        │   ┃  (•Bug fixes)        Mode switch                                          ·   air, as wide │  │ one release
        │   ┃                      A two-sided pill above the fields. …                 ·   as the lanes │  │ = one entry in
        │   ┃                      ╭ picture ────────────────────────╮                  ·   on the left  │  │   Changelog.json
        │   ┃                      ╰─────────────────────────────────╯                  ·                │  │
        │   │                      Also new 1                        ⌄                  ·                │  │
        │   │                      ─────────────────────────────────────                ·                │  │
        │   │                      Improvements 3                    ⌄                  ·                │  │
        │   │                        • Softer auto-fill glow ▭   ← a line with a picture                 │  │
        │   │                      (o) Shipped by  Mili                                 ·                │  ┘
        │  ◖│  November 9, 2026    Every node on its own tab.                           ·                │  every release uses
        │   │  0.0.9               ╭ picture ╮  …  New 3 ›  Fixes 3 ›                   ·                │  the same template
        │   •                      Show 0.0.7 and earlier ⌄                                              │  "older" row
        └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

    THE STEM. Our team is called Sunflower, so the rail on the left is the stem of the sunflower in the header:
      · The flower sits above the rail; its stem curves down and lands exactly on the rail (x 4‥6 of the rail lane).
      · Every release has a LEAF where a timeline usually has a dot. It is grey until the release is reached.
      · While you read downwards the rail turns green behind you ("Trail") and the leaf of the release you are
        reading travels down with its date, which stays in view like a sticky header ("Pin", "Node").
      WhatsNewWindow.xaml.cs does the moving; it looks for the parts named Pin, Node, NodeOn and Trail.

    Four lanes per release (the Grid in the template "Release"):
      1. Rail ....... 27 wide: a 9 px slot with the grey line (1 px) and the green trail (2 px), then 18 px air.
                      The leaf joins the rail 20 px below the top of the release and points to the left, into the margin.
      2. Date lane .. 221 wide: date (14/22), version (Mono 12/18, Muted), then the badges (wrap after 196 px).
      3. Body ....... at most 592 wide, 80 px empty below before the next release.
      4. Air ........ at most 248 wide = lanes 1 + 2, so the body stands in the middle. In a narrow window the air
                      gives way first, then the body. (The window is 1240 wide: 1200 as in Paper + border + scroll bar.)

    Body, top to bottom:
      · headline ...... 32/38 SemiBold
      · picture ....... optional ("image" on the release), 40 above and below
      · summary ....... 17/28 Muted, 14 below the headline
      · features ...... every "new" item with a text or picture: 56 above, title 22/30 SemiBold, text 16/26 (10 below
                        the title), picture 32 below the text
      · lists ......... "Also new" (or "New"), "Improvements", "Fixes" as folds: a 56 px head with title, count and
                        chevron, a hairline between them. Open in the newest release, closed in older ones.
      · shipped by .... optional ("by"): round photos (36 px, overlapping by 10), "Shipped by", the names in handwriting.

    A LIST LINE WITH A PICTURE ("image" on an improved or fixed item) gets a dashed underline and a tiny thumbnail.
      · hover → the preview card (template "Peek"): kind, title, text, a mini view of the picture, version and date
      · click → the large view (the Grid "Viewer" at the end of this file); the big pictures open it as well

    Badges: Feature (blue dot), Improvement (green) and Bug fixes (red) are worked out from the item types;
    words from "tags" follow with a grey dot. White pill with a hairline, text 12/18 Medium, 6 px between them.

    Not taken over from Paper: letter-spacing (WPF text has none) and the web font of the handwriting –
    "Hand" below falls back to handwriting fonts that ship with Windows.
-->
<Window x:Class="Conduit.WhatsNewWindow"
        xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:local="clr-namespace:Conduit"
        Title="What's new"
        Width="1240" Height="860" MinWidth="760" MinHeight="480"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        Icon="{StaticResource LogoImage}"
        FontFamily="{StaticResource Sans}" FontSize="13"
        Foreground="{StaticResource Ink}" Background="{StaticResource White}"
        UseLayoutRounding="True">

    <Window.Resources>

        <!-- Icons, drawn in a 12 × 12 box (PathIcon scales them). The close cross comes from App.xaml. -->
        <Geometry x:Key="Geo.Chevron">M3,4.5 L6,7.5 L9,4.5</Geometry>
        <Geometry x:Key="Geo.Expand">M7,2 H10 V5 M5,10 H2 V7 M10,2 L6.8,5.2 M2,10 L5.2,6.8</Geometry>

        <!-- ── The plant ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
             Greens of stem and leaves. The leaf of a release is drawn in a 30 × 20 box; its base – the point
             that sits on the rail – is at (26, 13), the tip points up and to the left. Three layers: the whole
             leaf, its darker lower half, the midrib. -->
        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Stem" Color="#6FA862" />
        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Leaf" Color="#A9D39B" />
        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="LeafShade" Color="#8DC27D" />
        <SolidColorBrush x:Key="LeafOffShade" Color="#D5D9E0" />
        <Geometry x:Key="Geo.Leaf">M26,13 C23.72,3.83 11.73,1.68 3.72,4.04 C8.79,11.16 17.78,17.33 26,13 Z</Geometry>
        <Geometry x:Key="Geo.LeafShade">M26,13 C18.38,9.38 10.27,7.1 3.72,4.04 C8.79,11.16 17.78,17.33 26,13 Z</Geometry>
        <Geometry x:Key="Geo.LeafRib">M26,13 C18.38,9.38 10.27,7.1 5.24,4.76</Geometry>

        <!-- The names after "Shipped by". Fonts that ship with Windows; put an own font first to change the hand. -->
        <FontFamily x:Key="Hand">Ink Free, Segoe Script, Segoe Print</FontFamily>

        <!-- 22/30 SemiBold: the title of a feature. -->
        <Style x:Key="Heading" TargetType="TextBlock">
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="22" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold" />
            <Setter Property="LineHeight" Value="30" />
            <Setter Property="LineStackingStrategy" Value="BlockLineHeight" />
            <Setter Property="TextWrapping" Value="Wrap" />
        </Style>

        <!-- 16/26: running text. A line break in the JSON text (\n) is shown as one. -->
        <Style x:Key="Copy" TargetType="TextBlock">
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="16" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource Body}" />
            <Setter Property="LineHeight" Value="26" />
            <Setter Property="LineStackingStrategy" Value="BlockLineHeight" />
            <Setter Property="TextWrapping" Value="Wrap" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Mono 11/16, Muted: the small capital lines ("NEWEST FIRST", "IMPROVEMENT", "0.1.0 · NOV 12").
             The capitals are in the text itself – WPF cannot transform the case. -->
        <Style x:Key="Tiny" TargetType="TextBlock">
            <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource Mono}" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="11" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource Muted}" />
            <Setter Property="LineHeight" Value="16" />
            <Setter Property="LineStackingStrategy" Value="BlockLineHeight" />
        </Style>

        <!-- A button that shows only its content (fold heads, "Show … and earlier", the close button). -->
        <ControlTemplate x:Key="Bare" TargetType="ButtonBase">
            <Border Background="Transparent">
                <ContentPresenter />
            </Border>
        </ControlTemplate>

        <!-- Dashed underline of a list line that has a picture: 1 px, 3 px below the baseline, dashes 3 on / 2 off.
             Grey at rest, ink while the mouse is over the line. -->
        <TextDecorationCollection x:Key="Dash.Rest">
            <TextDecoration Location="Underline" PenOffset="3" PenOffsetUnit="Pixel" PenThicknessUnit="Pixel">
                <TextDecoration.Pen>
                    <Pen Brush="{StaticResource Faint}" Thickness="1">
                        <Pen.DashStyle>
                            <DashStyle Dashes="3,2" />
                        </Pen.DashStyle>
                    </Pen>
                </TextDecoration.Pen>
            </TextDecoration>
        </TextDecorationCollection>
        <TextDecorationCollection x:Key="Dash.Hover">
            <TextDecoration Location="Underline" PenOffset="3" PenOffsetUnit="Pixel" PenThicknessUnit="Pixel">
                <TextDecoration.Pen>
                    <Pen Brush="{StaticResource Ink}" Thickness="1">
                        <Pen.DashStyle>
                            <DashStyle Dashes="3,2" />
                        </Pen.DashStyle>
                    </Pen>
                </TextDecoration.Pen>
            </TextDecoration>
        </TextDecorationCollection>

        <!-- ── Badge under the date ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
             White pill, 24 high: hairline, padding 8 | 9 × 2, a 6 px dot, text 12/18 Medium.
             6 px to the next badge and to the next row. The dot is grey by default (a word from "tags");
             the three automatic kinds get their colour below. -->
        <DataTemplate x:Key="Badge" DataType="{x:Type local:Badge}">
            <Border Margin="0,0,6,6" Padding="8,2,9,2" CornerRadius="12" Background="{StaticResource White}"
                    BorderBrush="{StaticResource Line}" BorderThickness="1">
                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal">
                    <Ellipse x:Name="Spot" Width="6" Height="6" Margin="0,0,6,0" VerticalAlignment="Center" Fill="{StaticResource Faint}" />
                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding Text}" FontSize="12" FontWeight="Medium" Foreground="{StaticResource Body}"
                               LineHeight="18" LineStackingStrategy="BlockLineHeight" />
                </StackPanel>
            </Border>
            <DataTemplate.Triggers>
                <DataTrigger Binding="{Binding Kind}" Value="feature">
                    <Setter TargetName="Spot" Property="Fill" Value="{StaticResource Blue}" />
                </DataTrigger>
                <DataTrigger Binding="{Binding Kind}" Value="improvement">
                    <Setter TargetName="Spot" Property="Fill" Value="{StaticResource Green}" />
                </DataTrigger>
                <DataTrigger Binding="{Binding Kind}" Value="fix">
                    <Setter TargetName="Spot" Property="Fill" Value="{StaticResource Red}" />
                </DataTrigger>
            </DataTemplate.Triggers>
        </DataTemplate>

        <!-- ── Picture frame ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
             Its data is the address of the picture. Two layers: the grey shape (radius 12) and the picture cut
             to that shape. A wide picture is scaled down to the body width; a small one keeps its size and sits
             in the middle of the grey. -->
        <DataTemplate x:Key="Picture">
            <Grid>
                <Border x:Name="Shape" CornerRadius="12" Background="{StaticResource Page}" />
                <Image Source="{Binding}" Stretch="Uniform" StretchDirection="DownOnly" HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                       RenderOptions.BitmapScalingMode="HighQuality">
                    <Image.OpacityMask>
                        <VisualBrush Visual="{Binding ElementName=Shape}" />
                    </Image.OpacityMask>
                </Image>
            </Grid>
        </DataTemplate>

        <!-- ── Feature: a "new" item with a text or picture. 56 px above, text 10 below the title, picture 32 below.
             A click on the picture opens the large view. ── -->
        <DataTemplate x:Key="Feature" DataType="{x:Type local:Change}">
            <StackPanel Margin="0,56,0,0">
                <TextBlock Text="{Binding Title}" Style="{StaticResource Heading}" />
                <TextBlock Text="{Binding Text}" Margin="0,10,0,0" Style="{StaticResource Copy}"
                           Visibility="{Binding Text, Converter={StaticResource VisibleWhen}}" />
                <ContentControl Margin="0,32,0,0" Content="{Binding Picture}" ContentTemplate="{StaticResource Picture}" Focusable="False"
                                Cursor="Hand" MouseLeftButtonUp="OnPictureClicked"
                                Visibility="{Binding Picture, Converter={StaticResource VisibleWhen}}" />
            </StackPanel>
        </DataTemplate>

        <!-- ── Preview card: what a list line with a picture shows while the mouse rests on it ───────────────
             It is the tool tip of the line, restyled – so Windows opens, places and closes it.
             336 wide, white, radius 16, hairline, soft shadow. Inside (padding 16): the kind in small capitals,
             title 15/22 SemiBold, the text 14/22 if there is one, a 136 px mini view of the picture (radius 10),
             a hairline, then version and date on the left and "Click to enlarge" on the right.
             It sits 10 px under the line, flush with its left edge (the offsets take the 24 px of transparent
             room for the shadow back). It fades in over 160 ms and rises 6 px while doing so. -->
        <Style x:Key="Peek" TargetType="ToolTip">
            <Setter Property="OverridesDefaultStyle" Value="True" />
            <Setter Property="HasDropShadow" Value="False" />
            <Setter Property="Placement" Value="Bottom" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalOffset" Value="-24" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalOffset" Value="-14" />
            <Setter Property="FontFamily" Value="{StaticResource Sans}" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource Ink}" />
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <Setter.Value>
                    <ControlTemplate TargetType="ToolTip">
                        <Grid x:Name="Card" Width="336" Margin="24,24,24,40">
                            <Grid.RenderTransform>
                                <TranslateTransform />
                            </Grid.RenderTransform>
                            <!-- the shadow lives on its own layer behind the card -->
                            <Border CornerRadius="16" Background="{StaticResource White}">
                                <Border.Effect>
                                    <DropShadowEffect BlurRadius="40" ShadowDepth="14" Direction="270" Color="#0B0D12" Opacity="0.14" />
                                </Border.Effect>
                            </Border>
                            <Border CornerRadius="16" Padding="16" Background="{StaticResource White}"
                                    BorderBrush="{StaticResource Line}" BorderThickness="1">
                                <StackPanel>
                                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding Label}" Style="{StaticResource Tiny}" />
                                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding Title}" Margin="0,4,0,0" FontSize="15" FontWeight="SemiBold"
                                               LineHeight="22" LineStackingStrategy="BlockLineHeight" TextWrapping="Wrap" />
                                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding Text}" Margin="0,4,0,0" FontSize="14" Foreground="{StaticResource Body}"
                                               LineHeight="22" LineStackingStrategy="BlockLineHeight" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                               Visibility="{Binding Text, Converter={StaticResource VisibleWhen}}" />
                                    <!-- mini view: the picture fills the box and is cut to its round corners -->
                                    <Border Height="136" Margin="0,14,0,0" CornerRadius="10" Background="{StaticResource Page}">
                                        <Rectangle RadiusX="10" RadiusY="10" RenderOptions.BitmapScalingMode="HighQuality">
                                            <Rectangle.Fill>
                                                <ImageBrush ImageSource="{Binding Picture}" Stretch="UniformToFill" />
                                            </Rectangle.Fill>
                                        </Rectangle>
                                    </Border>
                                    <Border Margin="0,14,0,0" Padding="0,12,0,0" BorderBrush="{StaticResource Line}" BorderThickness="0,1,0,0">
                                        <DockPanel>
                                            <StackPanel DockPanel.Dock="Right" Orientation="Horizontal">
                                                <local:PathIcon Data="{StaticResource Geo.Expand}" Box="12" Width="12" Height="12" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                                                <TextBlock Text="Click to enlarge" Margin="6,0,0,0" FontSize="12" FontWeight="Medium"
                                                           LineHeight="16" LineStackingStrategy="BlockLineHeight" />
                                            </StackPanel>
                                            <TextBlock Text="{Binding Stamp}" Style="{StaticResource Tiny}" />
                                        </DockPanel>
                                    </Border>
                                </StackPanel>
                            </Border>
                        </Grid>
                        <ControlTemplate.Triggers>
                            <EventTrigger RoutedEvent="ToolTip.Opened">
                                <BeginStoryboard>
                                    <Storyboard>
                                        <DoubleAnimation Storyboard.TargetName="Card" Storyboard.TargetProperty="Opacity"
                                                         From="0" To="1" Duration="0:0:0.16" />
                                        <DoubleAnimation Storyboard.TargetName="Card"
                                                         Storyboard.TargetProperty="(UIElement.RenderTransform).(TranslateTransform.Y)"
                                                         From="6" To="0" Duration="0:0:0.16">
                                            <DoubleAnimation.EasingFunction>
                                                <CubicEase EasingMode="EaseOut" />
                                            </DoubleAnimation.EasingFunction>
                                        </DoubleAnimation>
                                    </Storyboard>
                                </BeginStoryboard>
                            </EventTrigger>
                        </ControlTemplate.Triggers>
                    </ControlTemplate>
                </Setter.Value>
            </Setter>
        </Style>

        <!-- ── One list line: [dot 5] 12 [text 16/26]. The dot sits on the first text line. 6 px to the next line.
             With a picture ("image" in the JSON) the words get a dashed underline and a 26 × 18 thumbnail follows
             the last word. The whole line is then a hand cursor: hover shows the preview card, a click the large
             view. Under the mouse the underline turns ink and the dot blue. ── -->
        <DataTemplate x:Key="ListLine" DataType="{x:Type local:Change}">
            <DockPanel x:Name="Row" Margin="0,0,0,6" Background="Transparent" MouseLeftButtonUp="OnPictureClicked"
                       ToolTipService.IsEnabled="{Binding HasPicture}" ToolTipService.InitialShowDelay="120" ToolTipService.ShowDuration="600000">
                <DockPanel.ToolTip>
                    <ToolTip Style="{StaticResource Peek}" />
                </DockPanel.ToolTip>
                <Ellipse x:Name="Bullet" DockPanel.Dock="Left" Width="5" Height="5" Margin="0,10,12,0" VerticalAlignment="Top" Fill="{StaticResource Faint}" />
                <TextBlock Style="{StaticResource Copy}">
                    <Run x:Name="Word" Text="{Binding Title, Mode=OneWay}" />
                    <InlineUIContainer BaselineAlignment="Center">
                        <Border Width="26" Height="18" Margin="5,0,0,0" CornerRadius="5" BorderBrush="{StaticResource Line}" BorderThickness="1"
                                RenderOptions.BitmapScalingMode="HighQuality"
                                Visibility="{Binding HasPicture, Converter={StaticResource VisibleWhen}}">
                            <Border.Background>
                                <ImageBrush ImageSource="{Binding Picture}" Stretch="UniformToFill" />
                            </Border.Background>
                        </Border>
                    </InlineUIContainer>
                </TextBlock>
            </DockPanel>
            <DataTemplate.Triggers>
                <DataTrigger Binding="{Binding HasPicture}" Value="True">
                    <Setter TargetName="Row" Property="Cursor" Value="Hand" />
                    <Setter TargetName="Word" Property="TextDecorations" Value="{StaticResource Dash.Rest}" />
                </DataTrigger>
                <MultiDataTrigger>
                    <MultiDataTrigger.Conditions>
                        <Condition Binding="{Binding HasPicture}" Value="True" />
                        <Condition Binding="{Binding IsMouseOver, ElementName=Row}" Value="True" />
                    </MultiDataTrigger.Conditions>
                    <Setter TargetName="Word" Property="TextDecorations" Value="{StaticResource Dash.Hover}" />
                    <Setter TargetName="Word" Property="Foreground" Value="{StaticResource Ink}" />
                    <Setter TargetName="Bullet" Property="Fill" Value="{StaticResource Blue}" />
                </MultiDataTrigger>
            </DataTemplate.Triggers>
        </DataTemplate>

        <!-- ── Fold: one list of a release that can be opened and closed ─────────────────────────────────────
             Head, 56 high: title 15/24 Medium, 8 px, the number of lines in Muted, the chevron at the far right
             (pointing right when closed, down when open). A hairline above every fold but the first.
             Lines: see "ListLine"; 20 px under the last one. -->
        <DataTemplate x:Key="Fold" DataType="{x:Type local:Fold}">
            <Border x:Name="Rule" BorderBrush="{StaticResource Line}" BorderThickness="0,1,0,0">
                <StackPanel>
                    <ToggleButton x:Name="Head" Height="56" Template="{StaticResource Bare}" Cursor="Hand" IsChecked="{Binding Open, Mode=OneTime}">
                        <DockPanel VerticalAlignment="Center">
                            <local:PathIcon x:Name="Arrow" DockPanel.Dock="Right" Data="{StaticResource Geo.Chevron}" Box="12" Width="14" Height="14"
                                            Foreground="{StaticResource Faint}" VerticalAlignment="Center" RenderTransformOrigin="0.5,0.5">
                                <local:PathIcon.RenderTransform>
                                    <RotateTransform Angle="-90" />
                                </local:PathIcon.RenderTransform>
                            </local:PathIcon>
                            <TextBlock FontSize="15" LineHeight="24" LineStackingStrategy="BlockLineHeight">
                                <Run Text="{Binding Title, Mode=OneWay}" FontWeight="Medium" />
                                <Run Text="{Binding Count, Mode=OneWay}" Foreground="{StaticResource Muted}" />
                            </TextBlock>
                        </DockPanel>
                    </ToggleButton>
                    <ItemsControl x:Name="Lines" Margin="0,0,0,14" ItemsSource="{Binding Items}" ItemTemplate="{StaticResource ListLine}"
                                  Focusable="False" Visibility="Collapsed" />
                </StackPanel>
            </Border>
            <DataTemplate.Triggers>
                <DataTrigger Binding="{Binding First}" Value="True">
                    <Setter TargetName="Rule" Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
                </DataTrigger>
                <Trigger SourceName="Head" Property="IsChecked" Value="True">
                    <Setter TargetName="Lines" Property="Visibility" Value="Visible" />
                    <Setter TargetName="Arrow" Property="RenderTransform">
                        <Setter.Value>
                            <RotateTransform Angle="0" />
                        </Setter.Value>
                    </Setter>
                </Trigger>
            </DataTemplate.Triggers>
        </DataTemplate>

        <!-- ── Face in "Shipped by": a 36 px photo with a white 2 px ring (40 in total).
             Every face moves 10 px over the one before it. No photo → the first letter on grey. ── -->
        <DataTemplate x:Key="Face" DataType="{x:Type local:Author}">
            <Grid Width="40" Height="40" Margin="-10,0,0,0" ToolTip="{Binding Name}">
                <Ellipse Fill="{StaticResource White}" />
                <Ellipse Margin="2" Fill="{StaticResource Chip}" />
                <TextBlock Text="{Binding Initial}" FontSize="14" FontWeight="SemiBold" Foreground="{StaticResource Muted}"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                <Ellipse Margin="2" RenderOptions.BitmapScalingMode="HighQuality"
                         Visibility="{Binding Photo, Converter={StaticResource VisibleWhen}}">
                    <Ellipse.Fill>
                        <ImageBrush ImageSource="{Binding Photo}" Stretch="UniformToFill" />
                    </Ellipse.Fill>
                </Ellipse>
            </Grid>
        </DataTemplate>

        <!-- ══ One release: rail | date lane | body | air ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════
             The names Pin, Node, NodeOn and Trail are used by WhatsNewWindow.xaml.cs for the stem that grows. -->
        <DataTemplate x:Key="Release" DataType="{x:Type local:Release}">
            <Grid>
                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="27" />
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="221" />
                    <!-- the body takes what there is up to 592; only then the air on the right gets its share -->
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="1000*" MaxWidth="592" />
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*" MaxWidth="248" />
                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

                <!-- 1 · Rail. "Line": the grey line down to the next release (x 4‥5).
                         "Trail": the part of it that has turned green (x 4‥6) – 1 px tall, stretched from code.
                         "Node": the leaf, grey; "NodeOn" is the same leaf in green, faded in once the release is reached.
                         The leaf's base (26, 13 in its box) lands on x 5, y 20 of the release. -->
                <Grid Width="9" HorizontalAlignment="Left">
                    <Rectangle x:Name="Line" Width="1" Margin="4,0,0,0" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Fill="{StaticResource SkeletonLight}" />
                    <Rectangle x:Name="Trail" Width="2" Height="1" Margin="4,0,0,0" HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Top"
                               Fill="{StaticResource Stem}">
                        <Rectangle.RenderTransform>
                            <ScaleTransform ScaleY="0" />
                        </Rectangle.RenderTransform>
                    </Rectangle>
                    <Canvas x:Name="Node" Width="0" Height="0" Margin="-21,7,0,0" HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Top">
                        <Path Data="{StaticResource Geo.Leaf}" Fill="{StaticResource Line}" />
                        <Path Data="{StaticResource Geo.LeafShade}" Fill="{StaticResource LeafOffShade}" />
                        <Path Data="{StaticResource Geo.LeafRib}" Stroke="{StaticResource Dot}" StrokeThickness="0.8"
                              StrokeStartLineCap="Round" StrokeEndLineCap="Round" />
                        <Canvas x:Name="NodeOn" Opacity="0">
                            <Path Data="{StaticResource Geo.Leaf}" Fill="{StaticResource Leaf}" />
                            <Path Data="{StaticResource Geo.LeafShade}" Fill="{StaticResource LeafShade}" />
                            <Path Data="{StaticResource Geo.LeafRib}" Stroke="{StaticResource Stem}" StrokeThickness="0.8"
                                  StrokeStartLineCap="Round" StrokeEndLineCap="Round" />
                        </Canvas>
                    </Canvas>
                </Grid>

                <!-- 2 · Date lane: 8 px down so the date sits on the line of the headline -->
                <StackPanel x:Name="Pin" Grid.Column="1" Margin="0,8,0,0" VerticalAlignment="Top">
                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding DateText}" FontSize="14" LineHeight="22" LineStackingStrategy="BlockLineHeight" />
                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding Version}" Margin="0,2,0,0" FontFamily="{StaticResource Mono}" FontSize="12"
                               Foreground="{StaticResource Muted}" LineHeight="18" LineStackingStrategy="BlockLineHeight" />
                    <!-- 196 px of badges + the 6 px every badge carries on its right; -6 eats the gap under the last row -->
                    <ItemsControl Width="202" Margin="0,12,0,-6" HorizontalAlignment="Left" ItemsSource="{Binding Badges}"
                                  ItemTemplate="{StaticResource Badge}" Focusable="False">
                        <ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                            <ItemsPanelTemplate>
                                <WrapPanel />
                            </ItemsPanelTemplate>
                        </ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                    </ItemsControl>
                </StackPanel>

                <!-- 3 · Body -->
                <StackPanel Grid.Column="2" Margin="0,0,0,80">
                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding Headline}" FontSize="32" FontWeight="SemiBold"
                               LineHeight="38" LineStackingStrategy="BlockLineHeight" TextWrapping="Wrap" />
                    <!-- picture of the release: 40 above; 26 below + the 14 of the summary = 40 -->
                    <ContentControl Margin="0,40,0,26" Content="{Binding Picture}" ContentTemplate="{StaticResource Picture}" Focusable="False"
                                    Cursor="Hand" MouseLeftButtonUp="OnPictureClicked"
                                    Visibility="{Binding Picture, Converter={StaticResource VisibleWhen}}" />
                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding Summary}" Margin="0,14,0,0" FontSize="17" Foreground="{StaticResource Muted}"
                               LineHeight="28" LineStackingStrategy="BlockLineHeight" TextWrapping="Wrap" />

                    <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Features}" ItemTemplate="{StaticResource Feature}" Focusable="False" />

                    <!-- the lists, 32 px below (their first head brings 16 px of its own air). Hidden when there is none. -->
                    <ItemsControl Margin="0,32,0,0" ItemsSource="{Binding Folds}" ItemTemplate="{StaticResource Fold}" Focusable="False"
                                  Visibility="{Binding Folds, Converter={StaticResource VisibleWhen}}" />

                    <!-- Shipped by: [faces] 12 "Shipped by" 9 [names]. The faces start 8 px in because the first one
                         also moves 10 px left and carries its 2 px ring. Hidden when the release names nobody. -->
                    <StackPanel Margin="0,32,0,0" Orientation="Horizontal" Visibility="{Binding Authors, Converter={StaticResource VisibleWhen}}">
                        <ItemsControl Margin="8,0,0,0" VerticalAlignment="Center" ItemsSource="{Binding Authors}"
                                      ItemTemplate="{StaticResource Face}" Focusable="False">
                            <ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                                <ItemsPanelTemplate>
                                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" />
                                </ItemsPanelTemplate>
                            </ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                        </ItemsControl>
                        <TextBlock Text="Shipped by" Margin="10,0,0,0" FontSize="15" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                        <TextBlock Text="{Binding ByText}" Margin="9,0,0,0" FontFamily="{StaticResource Hand}" FontSize="24" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                    </StackPanel>
                </StackPanel>
            </Grid>

            <!-- The newest release is the top of the rail: the grey line starts at its leaf instead of above it
                 (above it is the stem of the flower), and its leaf is green when the window opens. -->
            <DataTemplate.Triggers>
                <DataTrigger Binding="{Binding IsLatest}" Value="True">
                    <Setter TargetName="Line" Property="Margin" Value="4,20,0,0" />
                    <Setter TargetName="NodeOn" Property="Opacity" Value="1" />
                </DataTrigger>
            </DataTemplate.Triggers>
        </DataTemplate>
